From: steinmarder W10 perf-query track
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] drm/radeon: add DRM_RADEON_PERF_QUERY ioctl

Unprivileged batch readback of the Evergreen / TeraScale-2 perf-counter
MMIO allowlist through the render node.  Replaces the CAP_SYS_ADMIN
debugfs path (out-of-tree radeon_sq_debugfs) for production Vulkan and
OpenGL clients (VK_KHR_performance_query, GL_AMD_performance_monitor).

Adds:
  - include/uapi/drm/radeon_drm.h:  struct drm_radeon_perf_query,
    DRM_RADEON_PERF_QUERY = 0x2e, RADEON_PERF_QUERY_* flags.
  - drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/perf_register_whitelist.h: closed allowlist
    of 13 perf-counter MMIO offsets with public AMD doc citations.
  - drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_perf_query.c: ioctl handler with
    optional pm_runtime_get_sync + DPM force-high guard for SCLK pinning.
  - drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon.h: prototype.
  - drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_drv.c: DRM_IOCTL_DEF_DRV entry.
  - drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/Makefile: build the new TU.

Family gate (CHIP_CEDAR..CHIP_ARUBA) lives inside the handler so
platforms outside Evergreen / Northern Islands return -EOPNOTSUPP.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 4.7
